########################################################################

DOCUMENT();      

loadMacros(
   "PGstandard.pl",     # Standard macros for PG language
   "MathObjects.pl",
   #"source.pl",        # allows code to be displayed on certain sites.
   #"PGcourse.pl",      # Customization file for the course
);

# Print problem number and point value (weight) for the problem
TEXT(beginproblem());

# Show which answers are correct and which ones are incorrect
$showPartialCorrectAnswers = 1;

##############################################################
#
#  Setup
#
#
Context("Numeric");


##############################################################
#
#  Text
#
#

Context()->texStrings;
BEGIN_TEXT


Let \(P\) be the partitions of the region \(R = [1,3] \times [2,5]\) into six \(1 \times 1\) squares. Define \(f(x,y) = xy^2\). $BR

Calculate the Riemann sum \(S_P^*(f)\) using the lower right corners as sample points.

$BR
$BR
\(S_P^*(f) = \) \{ans_rule(20)\}
$BR
$BR

END_TEXT
Context()->normalStrings;

##############################################################
#
#  Answers
#
#

$sum = "145" ;
ANS(num_cmp($sum));

ENDDOCUMENT();        
